UI_SCorpsResourceRuleBox_0 = "<font color='#ccba7a'>Resource Planet: </font><br><font color='#00FF00'>1.</font>If you are in a Guild, you can compete with others to control this planet. Upon taking control, all ownership rights will go to your Guild.<br><font color='#00FF00'>2.</font> All defense buildings on the planet can be upgraded using the Guild's wealth. The higher the level, the better the upgrades will be.<font color='#00FF00'> (accessible only by Generals)</font><br><font color='#00FF00'>3.</font> The higher the level of the Resource Planet base, the faster the ship production and Science Research rates of the controling Guilds. Additionally, the maximum number of fleets that can be stationed on the planet will increase.<font color='#00FF00'>(Garrison Resource Planet from the Guild "Territories" interface. Elite Guild members can garrison Resource Planets.)</font><br><font color='#00FF00'>4.</font> Once the Resource Bonus Planet is occupied, it will go into a protection phase for 3 days. After that time it goes into 1 day of battle, then 3 days of protection again, etc.<font color='#00FF00'>(If the Resource Planet is still contested when it goes into the protection phase, the battle goes into Overtime, and participants can no longer dispatch reinforcement fleets. Resource Planets under the protection phase cannot be attacked.)</font><br><font color='#00FF00'>5.</font>Ships can only be garrisoned and recalled from the Resource Planets outside of combat. Battles that go into Overtime will continue until either all fleets on one side of the battle are eliminated or when the battle has reached the maximum number of Rounds allowed (Stalemate). If the result is a stalemate, the defending side wins and the surviving invader fleets return to their respective bases. If the invaders win, the protection phase of the Resource Planet resets back to the full duration of 3 days. If the defending side wins, the protection phase continues with its countdown to expiry.<font color='#00FF00'>(Players can select their own fleets stationed at the Resource Planets and choose to recall them from there.)</font>"

